{
  "_comment": "SALVAGE kit: a tow chain looped between two welded cleats - the tow is their livelihood, and the chain stays rigged. Seven link boxes alternate flat and upright the way real links do, sag on a shallow curve between the cleat horns (each link is tilted to follow the slope under it), wander a centimetre either side of the line, and alternate WELD-dark and rust: a chain assembled from two chains. The cleats are the hook's grammar - posts of different height on welded pads - because the same crew made both. Long axis Z with the cleats at 0.40 of a cell out, footprint raised to 0.92, so consecutive plates of one run read as chain rigged the length of an edge.",
